---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { ProgressTransfer } from '../components/games/ProgressTransfer';
import { GENERATORS, availableGenerators } from '../lib/generators/registry';
import { CATEGORY_LABELS, CATEGORIES } from '../lib/types';
import { DAILY_SET_SIZE, DAILY_QUOTA } from '../lib/daily';
import { TIME_MODES } from '../lib/modes';

const available = availableGenerators();
const unavailable = GENERATORS.filter((g) => !g.available);
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{ title: 'About', description: 'What this is, how the drills are built, and what is deliberately missing.' }}
>
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    A daily practice tool for an Asian exotic-options desk. It tests the two things that get rusty
    fastest and are hardest to fake: mental arithmetic under mild time pressure, and recall of the
    market conventions and structures the desk trades.
  </p>

  <h2>How the daily set is built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>{DAILY_SET_SIZE} questions</strong>, mixed across five categories rather than blocked, because that is what a trading day looks like.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Generated from today's date.</strong> The whole set is a pure function of the date, so
      every visitor sees the same questions today. Nothing is fetched, so it cannot go stale mid-day.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Weighted toward exotics.</strong> The quota is{' '}
      {CATEGORIES.map((c) => `${CATEGORY_LABELS[c]} ${DAILY_QUOTA[c]}`).join(', ')}.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Every answer comes with the method.</strong> Feedback gives the correct value, the
      reasoning, a rule of thumb to memorise, and the source. A right answer reached the wrong way
      is still worth correcting.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Time modes</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Budget</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {TIME_MODES.map((m) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{m.label}</td>
          <td class="tt-mono">{m.secondsPerQuestion === null ? 'untimed' : `${m.secondsPerQuestion}s / question`}</td>
          <td>{m.description}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Generators in the pool</h2>
  <p class="tt-citation">
    {available.length} active, across {CATEGORIES.length} groups. Sub-group only applies inside Asia
    Derivatives, where listed contracts, OTC exotics and the vol surface are kept apart.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Generator</th><th>Group</th><th>Sub-group</th><th>Tier</th><th>Tests</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {available.map((g) => (
        <tr>
          <td class="tt-mono">{g.id}</td>
          <td>{CATEGORY_LABELS[g.category]}</td>
          <td class="tt-mono">{g.subgroup ?? '—'}</td>
          <td class="tt-mono">{g.tier}</td>
          <td>{g.about}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {unavailable.length > 0 ? (
    <>
      <h3>Disabled generators</h3>
      {unavailable.map((g) => (
        <p class="tt-stale">
          <strong class="tt-mono">{g.id}</strong> — {g.unavailableReason}
        </p>
      ))}
    </>
  ) : null}

  <h2>What is deliberately missing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No leaderboard, no accounts, no server.</strong> The site is static. The competitive
      element is against your own personal best. Scores are not transmitted anywhere, which also
      means they cannot be compared between users.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No streaks.</strong> Excluded by decision. Progress is measured by per-category
      accuracy and personal bests instead, which say something about skill rather than about habit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No live market data.</strong> Levels are frozen in the repository. Conversion and
      triangulation questions supply the rate in the question, so they never depend on a stale
      number. The one drill that would ask you to recall a level is disabled until the data has been
      verified.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No pricing library.</strong> The drills test conventions, directions and rules of
      thumb, not Greeks computed from a model.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Progress is stored in this browser's local storage. It does not follow you to another device and
    clearing site data will clear it. Use the panel below to keep a backup.
  </p>
  <ProgressTransfer client:load />

  <h2>Known gaps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The ticker drill covers SGX names only. Hong Kong, Japan and Australia need their own verified datasets before those rows can be added.</li>
    <li>The ASX market page carries an unverified daylight-saving caveat, so ASX session-time questions are not asked.</li>
    <li>FX levels are illustrative rather than verified.</li>
  </ul>
</StarlightPage>
